    "type": "question",
    "label": "24",
    "prompt": "Frank bought 2.75 m of wire at 68 cents per metre. What was the cost?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$1.87$",
      "worked": "68 cents per metre is $\\$0.68$ per metre.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2.75\\times0.68&=\\frac{275}{100}\\times\\frac{68}{100}\\\\2.75\\times0.68&=\\frac{18700}{10000}\\\\2.75\\times0.68&=1.87\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe cost was $\\$1.87$.",
